\f1\fs22 Constable Sman came top of his academy class in almost everything. But he didn\'92t come anywhere near as top-in-the-class as he came in Demographically Sensitive Culling. His scores were so good, upon graduation he could shoot and kill almost anyone he pleased, so long as he killed sufficient others to make his culling score demographically neutral. If, for example he wanted to kill an able-bodied Caucasian male in his thirties, he could calculate to sixteen points how many others he\'92d need to kill across a statistically acceptable proportionate number of people to balance the carnage across all demographics, so no one could sue prejudice for killing his original target. In the famous case of Purple Shirts versus the People of East Ulyssia, claims that Sman was colourist were summarily thrown out of court when his legal team provided detailed cop-cam evidence of the number of his kills on that expedition, which conclusively showed his killing spree was not prejudiced against wearers of purple, or any other colour for that matter. Further, they showed beyond a doubt, he was found blameless of vilifying purple-wearing, tall, basketball-playing, balding women who abhorred mahjong and drinking tea in the afternoons.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>When asked how he did it, he oft quoted a sociopath in an old movie: \'91I just have to kill a lot of people.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sman\'92s skills became highly sought by police agencies all over, and he enjoyed the demographic variations of regions around the world. Finding the final trains-potting Inuit in Surrey who enjoyed riding broken bicycles was a challenge he especially enjoyed rising to, but after a number of years and a stellar career of never blotting his spreadsheets, he grew homesick for East Ulyssia, for, as he would sometimes confess to his closest friends, \'91There are too many fuckin\'92 Cloudborne where I come from.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He was almost found guilty in one case where it was shown he\'92d fallen short of his quota in one significant demographic, which he easily rectified by blowing the head off the prosecutor. Case dismissed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>So, when the cop with the sniper gun says, \'91I can cover it, sir,\'92 you know he can cover it.\
